 progress  just because your healer got teleported  into a pool of curse blood and your  party died it's not safe coming it's  playing tactically when you're starting  your character you'll get the option  taking perks these lives should depend  on what kind of character you'll be  playing but for first-timers I really  think you should take pet pal and not  just because talking to animals is cool  as hell the ability to communicate with  your beastly brethren can make your life  easier  it would allow you to avoid some tricky  areas and uncover secrets I managed to  convince a pack of dogs not to rip my  throat out just by talking to the Alpha  and rats dwelling in dungeons and sewers  have kindly warned me about traps and  ambushes before I've delved deeper into  the darkness sure it takes a perks lot  but it's worth its weight in gold and  really without it you're missing out on  some great little distractions as well  as hearing voice actors tried to get  across what a dog's speaking English  might sound like I think I love you  [Music]  when a character in your party dies the  only way to bring them back is to use a  Resurrection scroll they're quite rare  an invaluable for turning combat around  and bringing your party back to full  strength while some of the encounters in  the early game are tricky they can often  be beaten with a bit of trial and error  and some use of saves as the game goes  on though some of the battles can become  drawn-out battles with characters on  slivers of Health just holding on to  their last breaths of life this is when  you need those scrolls during the course  of a 30 to 40 minute fight your  character might go down a number of  times and in divinity original sin to  being one guy down in a fight can change  everything  also make sure that every member of your  party is carrying at least one at all  times there's no point having your main  squeeze carrying them around because if  they go down they'll take all the  scrolls with them  [Music]  it's important to stay healthy in the  world of river lon danger is around  every corner when you build your party  the members will give you the option on  how they're built I recommend taking a  healer to keep you topped up in combat  but you've got to stay perky while  exploring the world as well especially  with all the traps ambushes poison  plants fires and exploding vents that  you'll come across save your potions for  battle instead carry plenty of food  someone even have bonus status effects  if you can find a bed you can let each  party member catch 40 winks and that  will slowly refill their health bar the  best way to heal out of combat though is  to use a bed roll the ship that you  spawn on will have a few of these so  make sure to take them all as they're  not unlimited use when you use them out  in the world you will refill your  party's health back to full and gain the  rested status effect for a gross looking  sleeping bag these are super valuable  items so make sure you keep an eye out  for them when you're out in the world or  talking to traders it's important to get  your beauty sleep after all a big part  of the divinity original sin series is  your command over the elements so  experiment with spells abilities and  environments to give you an upper hand  in battle most the abilities will create  some effect or another especially if you  have a specialist spell caster like a  Pyromancer or an arrow mansur water can  be electrified oil can be set ablaze  fire can be turned to steam to block  sight steam clouds can be filled with  poison or lightning characters that are  wet and more susceptible to being frozen  or stunned characters who are decaying  will be heard by healing a lot of this  knowledge will come with experience and  a little experimentation so don't be  afraid to play around with your options  before you know it you'll be training  crazy elemental reactions and creating  cursed clouds of doomed blood that shoot  lightning  the world of divinity original sin - is  dense massive and full of awesome things  to discover so if you find that the  tricky combat is preventing you from  experience all those things then don't  be afraid to turn the difficulty down to  explore a mode the classic mode on  divinity is still a brutal way to play  but in Explorer mode the focus is much  more on well exploring getting a chance  to talk to characters and make your own  way around the world discovering things  as you go and once you feel like a  lightning spewing fire throwing  backstabbing axe wielding badass there's  nothing stopping you from going back and  dining it back up to classic mode for a  nice challenge divinity is a game that  tries to put your experience first so  feel free to experience it in just the  way you want to so those are our hints  to get you started in your adventures in  divinity original sin - if you have any  hints yourself feel free to share them  and make sure you like the video if you  enjoyed it or found it helpful next week  I'll be putting up a feature on just why  I love this gem of a game so make sure  you subscribe so you don't miss that  until then I'm going to go play under  the 20 hours the game so I'll see you  next time  [Music]

